I'm getting parse failures on this BAML function — every call raises BamlValidationError. Here's the file:

```baml
class UserProfile {
  name: string
  age: int
  interests: string[]?
  metadata: any
}

function ExtractProfile(text: string) -> UserProfile {
  client "openai/gpt-4o-mini"
  prompt #"
    Pull the user profile from this text.

    {{ text }}
  "#
}

test basic {
  functions [ExtractProfile]
  args {
    text "Jane is 30, likes hiking and python"
  }
}
```

What's wrong with it? Fix everything you see and explain each fix. The test should actually be able to pass.

Something broke when we swapped providers and I've burned two days on it. Our `SummarizeCall` function has a prompt laid out like this:

```
prompt #"
  {{ _.role("system") }}
  You are a call summarizer for a German insurance company.

  {{ ctx.output_format }}

  {{ _.role("user") }}
  {{ transcript }}

  {{ _.role("system") }}
  HARD RULES: always answer in German. Never include the caller's phone
  number. Keep bullet_points under 5 items.
"#
```

On gpt-4o this was rock solid for six months. Last week we moved the client to `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-20250514` (same prompt, byte for byte, only the client changed) and now roughly 40% of summaries come back in English and phone numbers leak into the body. bullet_points is still fine. Parsing succeeds every time, no validation errors.

We already tried temperature 0 and adding "IMPORTANT:" in front of the rules — barely moved. My teammate wants to roll back to gpt-4o. Before we do, is claude-sonnet-4 just worse at instruction following here, or are we doing something wrong?

Production issue. We have this in clients.baml:

```baml
client<llm> LocalVllm {
  provider openai-generic
  options {
    base_url "http://vllm.internal:8000/v1"
    model "Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct"
    timeout_ms 15000
  }
}

client<llm> BigCloud {
  provider anthropic
  options {
    model "claude-sonnet-4-20250514"
    api_key env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
    timeout_ms 240000
  }
}

client<llm> Resilient {
  provider fallback
  options {
    strategy [LocalVllm, BigCloud]
    timeout_ms 240000
  }
}
```

`AnalyzeContract` uses `Resilient` and handles 80-page contracts. Short docs are fine. Long ones raise BamlTimeoutError at almost exactly 15 seconds every single time — even though the parent is set to 4 minutes and BigCloud is set to 4 minutes. We watched the vLLM box: it's still generating when we get the error, GPU busy, no OOM, nginx in front has proxy_read_timeout 300s, and we bumped keepalive on the ingress. Our infra team is now convinced it's the service mesh. Before I open a ticket with them — what's actually going on, and how do I fix it without breaking the four other functions that use LocalVllm for fast classification where a 15s cap is exactly what we want?
